Fixes and improvements
- CHECKOUT IDEMPOTENCY: nothing persists idempotency state on our side, so a double-clicked "Place Order" creates two orders.
  - apps/backend/src/core/workflows/types.ts has an `idempotent` config flag, but no workflow_execution table or idempotency-key storage backs it.
  - The Stripe provider passes idempotency keys to Stripe (apps/backend/src/providers/payment-stripe/stripe-provider.ts), which protects the charge but not the order record.
  - Same problem family as "investigate locking" below — decide the storage + locking strategy once and apply it to both.

